# [DD-13b.W23.5] w23_impl.md §3.2's OWED W23.3 row, never landed there
# (0 hits searched before this fixture existed) — SW7's ILL-FORMED-UTF-8
# ADVANCE RULE (`docs/spec/match_api.md` §3.1.1 / `docs/spec/
# rxt_format.md`'s `mc` paragraph), stated NORMATIVELY: from an empty
# match's own start `pos + 1`, then skip every byte in `0x80`-`0xBF`
# (a continuation byte with no lead byte before it).
#
# `x?` is NULLABLE (the advance rule only fires on a ZERO-WIDTH match,
# never on `en > st`) and the first subject `a\x80\x80\x80` is a lead-free
# run of three ill-formed continuation bytes AFTER a character — every byte
# of the run is skip-eligible.
#
#   WITH the rule: pos=0 matches empty, skip 1->4 in one step (three
#     continuation bytes), pos=4 matches empty (end of subject) — count 2.
#   WITHOUT it (naive `pos + 1` alone): pos=1,2,3 are searched too — a
#     python leg counts 5, and the C leg's search REFUSES pos=1 (K50's
#     caller-startpos guard), so neither leg reads 2.
#
# [K73] (2026-09-29) MOVED THIS FIXTURE'S SUBJECT. It used to be the bare
# `\x80\x80\x80` with an expected 2 (empty at 0, skip to 3, empty at 3).
# Since K73 a search at offset 0 does not attempt a match at a continuation
# byte — it starts at the first non-continuation byte, as libpcre2 does under
# PCRE2_MATCH_INVALID_UTF — so that subject's count is 1, and it no longer
# reached the advance rule at all. It stays as the SECOND case, now K73's own
# witness for the protocol. Both counts are libpcre2 10.46's under this same
# loop (`docs/dev/lanes/k73utf_evidence/k73_mc_findall_10.46.txt`).
pattern x?
encoding utf8
mc "a\x80\x80\x80" 2
mc "\x80\x80\x80" 1

# [K75] (D132, 2026-09-30) THE NON-EMPTY ARM. After a NON-EMPTY match the loop
# resumes at `<prefix>_next_pos(end - 1)` — from the match END, past every
# continuation byte — so a match ending before a STRAY continuation byte no
# longer parks the loop on it (K50 refuses a caller startpos there, and the
# loop used to stop and lose every later match). Every count below is
# libpcre2 10.48's, PCRE2_UTF|PCRE2_MATCH_INVALID_UTF driven through the same
# loop (`docs/dev/lanes/k75fix_report.md` carries the transcript and the
# pre-change counts).
#
# Subjects stay ASCII plus stray continuation bytes: leg C's python decodes a
# subject one character per BYTE, so a multi-byte character would make `.`
# count its two bytes separately and the leg could not be the second reader.
# `a` also carries one multi-byte subject, where the engine's own skip over a
# whole character and the loop's skip over the stray both fire.
pattern a
encoding utf8
mc "a\x80a" 2
mc "a\x80\x80a" 2
mc "a\xc3\xa9\x80a" 2

pattern .
encoding utf8
mc "a\x80a" 2

pattern a|
encoding utf8
mc "a\x80a" 3
mc "a\x80" 2
